		{"id":"279db89f075a26a6","type":"text","text":"Use String methods to extract labels, then assign them\n\n```python\nprefix  = path.split(\"/\")[-1].split(\"_\")[0]\n```","x":2691,"y":1121,"width":419,"height":202},
		{"id":"47ca2bcd579cbb25","type":"text","text":"Do Forward pass and compute loss","x":-2864,"y":1693,"width":250,"height":80},
		{"id":"ce604c8920884bd7","type":"text","text":"Do the 3 pillars of back","x":-2614,"y":1553,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"7ad10c5a846acc9b","type":"text","text":"Reading JSON: \n```python\nwith open(annotation_file, 'r') as f:            self.annotations = json.load(f)\n```\n\nIt's important to look at the nesting and structure of the JSON","x":3115,"y":81,"width":600,"height":240},
		{"id":"5c9c9173d620338e","type":"text","text":"CSV contains Metadata (labels).\nAssign each label to an image\n\nMetadata contains images' name and labels, use `iloc[idx, image/label]` to get one.","x":3115,"y":392,"width":600,"height":177},
		{"id":"63ee30876c233a4e","type":"text","text":"Train & Test Folders\nEach Label has Folder","x":1955,"y":899,"width":253,"height":76},
		{"id":"e52807a5a1088038","type":"text","text":"Looping over the labels' folders and assigning\n\n```python\nfor class_name, label in self.class_labels.items():\n\n            class_images = glob.glob(f\"{root_dir}/{class_name}/*.jpg\")  # Find all images\n\n            self.image_paths.extend(class_images)\n\n            self.labels.extend([label] * len(class_images))  # Assign labels\n```","x":2082,"y":1097,"width":420,"height":304},
		{"id":"168c7869d117e0dd","type":"text","text":"Non-Standard Structures\n","x":2775,"y":907,"width":250,"height":60},
